     "t": "code",
     "lang": "python",
     "code": "\"\"\"\nAn RLock (Reentrant Lock) is a lock that can be acquired multiple times by\nthe SAME thread without deadlocking. It maintains an ownership count and\na recursion level. The lock is only truly released when release() is called\nas many times as acquire() was called.\n\nthreading.RLock() has the same interface as Lock:\n  - acquire(blocking=True, timeout=-1)\n  - release()\n\nKey differences from Lock:\n  - Same thread can acquire it multiple times (recursive/reentrant).\n  - Must release the same number of times it was acquired.\n  - Only the owning thread can release it.\n  - Slightly slower than Lock due to ownership tracking.\n\nUse RLock when:\n  - A method that acquires the lock calls another method that also needs\n    the lock (recursive locking).\n  - You have a public API that uses locks, and methods call each other.\n\"\"\"\nimport threading\n\nclass ThreadSafeList:\n    \"\"\"List with reentrant locking for nested method calls.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._data = []\n        self._lock = threading.RLock()\n\n    def append(self, item):\n        with self._lock:\n            self._data.append(item)\n\n    def extend(self, items):\n        with self._lock:\n            # This calls append, which also acquires the lock.\n            # RLock allows this; a regular Lock would deadlock!\n            for item in items:\n                self.append(item)  # Nested lock acquisition\n\n    def get_snapshot(self):\n        with self._lock:\n            return list(self._data)\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        with self._lock:\n            return len(self._data)\n\nprint(\"Q280: RLocks\")\nts_list = ThreadSafeList()\nts_list.extend([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\nprint(f\"  After extend([1,2,3,4,5]): {ts_list.get_snapshot()}\")\nprint(f\"  Length: {len(ts_list)}\")\nprint(\"  RLock allows extend() to call append() without deadlocking\")\n\n# Show reentrant behavior\nrlock = threading.RLock()\nrlock.acquire()\nrlock.acquire()  # Same thread — no deadlock!\nprint(f\"  RLock acquired twice by same thread: OK\")\nrlock.release()\nrlock.release()\nprint(f\"  Released twice: fully unlocked\")\nprint()",
