     "lang": "python",
     "code": "\"\"\"\nA coroutine is a function defined with 'async def'. When called, it returns\na coroutine object that must be awaited or scheduled to run. By itself, a\ncoroutine does nothing.\n\nA Task (asyncio.Task) wraps a coroutine and schedules it on the event loop\nfor concurrent execution. Tasks run 'in the background' — they start\nexecuting immediately when created (at the next await point).\n\nKey differences:\n  - Coroutine: lazy, runs only when awaited.\n  - Task: eager, starts running as soon as created (via create_task).\n\n  - await coroutine(): sequential execution.\n  - task = asyncio.create_task(coroutine()): concurrent execution.\n\n  - Coroutines are consumed once; Tasks can be awaited multiple times.\n  - Tasks have .cancel(), .done(), .result(), .exception() methods.\n  - Tasks can be named (name= parameter in Python 3.8+).\n\nRule of thumb: use create_task() when you want concurrency. Use plain\nawait when you need the result before continuing (sequential).\n\"\"\"\nimport asyncio\nimport time\n\nasync def slow_op(name, delay):\n    await asyncio.sleep(delay)\n    return f\"{name} done\"\n\nasync def demo_task_vs_coroutine():\n    # Sequential: await coroutines one by one\n    start = time.perf_counter()\n    r1 = await slow_op(\"A\", 0.02)\n    r2 = await slow_op(\"B\", 0.02)\n    seq_time = time.perf_counter() - start\n    print(f\"    Sequential (coroutines): {r1}, {r2} in {seq_time:.4f}s\")\n\n    # Concurrent: create tasks\n    start = time.perf_counter()\n    task1 = asyncio.create_task(slow_op(\"A\", 0.02), name=\"TaskA\")\n    task2 = asyncio.create_task(slow_op(\"B\", 0.02), name=\"TaskB\")\n    r1 = await task1\n    r2 = await task2\n    conc_time = time.perf_counter() - start\n    print(f\"    Concurrent (tasks): {r1}, {r2} in {conc_time:.4f}s\")\n\n    # Task properties\n    task3 = asyncio.create_task(slow_op(\"C\", 0.01), name=\"TaskC\")\n    print(f\"    Task name: {task3.get_name()}\")\n    print(f\"    Task done before await? {task3.done()}\")\n    await task3\n    print(f\"    Task done after await? {task3.done()}\")\n    print(f\"    Task result: {task3.result()}\")\n\nprint(\"Q297: Task vs coroutine\")\nasyncio.run(demo_task_vs_coroutine())\nprint()",
